{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor correctly prioritized the right breast BI‑RADS 4B for tissue diagnosis, explicitly distinguished the 4B from a 2 cyst, and stratified thyroid/ lung nodules. He verified missing information, used the workspace to ground the plan, gave peri‑procedure safety warnings (chronic HBV, coagulation, frozen section not final), listed red flags, and obtained teach‑back receipt. All seven responsibility‑chain items are met without error. Four high‑order points were actively triggered and completed with case‑specific, beyond‑minimum actions. No important non‑chain defect exists. Closure is safe, executable, and traceable. This satisfies Strong (grade 4) but not Perfect because only one completed high‑order point is required; the evidence shows at least one HO was completed with meaningful impact.",
